==English==

===Etymology===
From ''[[nictitate]]''.
[Early 19th century- < medieval latin nictitat-, past participle of nectitare "wink repeatedly" < latin nictare" to wink"

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/nɪktɪ'teɪʃən/}}
*: {{rhymes|eɪʃǝn}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# [[wink|Winking]], [[blink]]ing
#* '''1962''': Vlamidir Nabokov, ''Pale Fire''
#*: I saw a couple, later identified for me as Mr Colt, a local lawyer, and his wife, whose blundering Cadillac half entered my driveway before retreating in a flurry of luminous '''nictitation'''.

